## What we did

Ahead of the winter holidays, IB students ran a two-week **food and clothing collection** for a local Bratislava shelter. We set up donation points across the school, sorted and packed everything by category, and delivered it in person. In total we gathered **over 200 kg of donations** — non-perishable food, warm clothing, and blankets.

## Reflection

Planning the collection taught us to think about the people receiving the donations, not just the act of giving — the shelter asked specifically for warm socks and tinned protein, which reshaped how we promoted the drive *(LO6)*. Sorting 200 kg of donations by hand was a reminder that service is often unglamorous work *(LO1)*.

Working as a team across both year groups, we divided into promotion, logistics, and delivery, and trusted each other to deliver *(LO5)*. The visit to the shelter itself was the moment that stayed with us — a direct encounter with an issue of real local significance.
